Univers42/Inception: find hellish where a 42 machine can actually keep it.

The Makefile hunts for an interpreter in five fixed system paths and stops at
parse time when none of them exists:

    Makefile:29: *** no usable hellish interpreter.  Stop.

On a 42 machine there is no root, so a hand-built or downloaded hellish lives
in the user's own bin -- /home/<login>/.local/bin/hellish here -- and the list
never looked there. `make`, `make setup`, `make test`, everything, refused to
run on the host that owns the project, while the same tree built fine inside
the born2root VM (where first-boot installs /usr/bin/hellish). Measured
2026-09-12 against upstream main (2e2962b): before, the error above; after,
SCRIPT_SH = /home/dlesieur/.local/bin/hellish and `make -n setup` expands.

`command -v` is consulted last, so a system install still wins and no existing
setup changes behaviour. The probe still has the final say: a candidate counts
only if it prints INC_SH=<its own path>.

born2root's own Makefile solved the same problem by asking the shell make was
launched from (tools/launcher_probe.sh); this is the smaller version of that.

Apply with:  git -C <inception> apply /path/to/this/file

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 9a701e9..b87ae79 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -6,8 +6,22 @@ export BUILDX_NO_DEFAULT_ATTESTATIONS = 1
 COMPOSE  = docker compose -f srcs/docker-compose.yml
 
 ifeq ($(origin SCRIPT_SH),undefined)
+# The five system paths are where a packaged hellish lands, and where the
+# containers find it. A hellish built or downloaded by hand lands in the
+# user's own bin -- on a 42 machine there is no root, so that is the ONLY
+# place it can be, and with the list stopping at /usr/local the Makefile
+# aborted at parse time on the very host that runs the project:
+#
+#     Makefile:29: *** no usable hellish interpreter.  Stop.
+#
+# `command -v` is asked last, so a system install still wins and nothing
+# about an existing setup changes; it only adds the case where hellish is on
+# PATH somewhere else (~/.local/bin here). The probe still decides: a
+# candidate is used only if it prints INC_SH=<path> for itself.
 _inc_cands := $(wildcard /bin/hellish /usr/bin/hellish /usr/local/bin/hellish \
-	/bin/hellish.real /usr/bin/hellish.real)
+	/bin/hellish.real /usr/bin/hellish.real) \
+	$(shell command -v hellish 2>/dev/null) \
+	$(shell command -v hellish.real 2>/dev/null)
 _inc_try    = $(filter INC_SH=%,$(shell $(1) tests/launcher_probe.sh 2>/dev/null))
 _inc_found := $(firstword $(foreach c,$(_inc_cands),$(call _inc_try,$(c))))
 SCRIPT_SH  := $(strip $(patsubst INC_SH=%,%,$(_inc_found)))
